problem:
Problem description
- There is a single-period fleet rental planning problem with truck types indexed by $$t \in \mathcal{T}$$ and cargo classes indexed by $$k \in \mathcal{K}$$.
- The planning horizon is represented by $$\mathcal{H}$$ and contains one rental planning period.
- The input provides a demand vector $$d_k$$ for each cargo class, a capacity matrix $$A_{t,k}$$ for each truck type and cargo class, and a per-kilometer rental cost vector $$c_t$$ for each truck type.
- The planning goal is to choose how many trucks of each type to rent so that all cargo demand is covered at minimum total rental cost.
- Some truck types may have different capacities across cargo classes, while others may have equal capacities across cargo classes as specified by the input data.
- Only whole trucks may be rented, and the rented fleet must be sufficient for every cargo class simultaneously.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_t$$: the nonnegative integer number of trucks of type $$t$$ to rent.
  - $$z$$: the minimized total rental cost, expressed per kilometer unless an explicit travel distance parameter is provided.

Input Format
{
  "sets": {
    "truck_types": {
      "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{T}$$",
      "dimension": "One-dimensional set",
      "description": "Set of available truck types."
    },
    "cargo_classes": {
      "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{K}$$",
      "dimension": "One-dimensional set",
      "description": "Set of cargo classes, such as $$\\{\\mathrm{ref},\\mathrm{dry}\\}$$."
    },
    "planning_horizon": {
      "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{H}$$",
      "dimension": "One-dimensional set",
      "description": "Single-period planning horizon."
    }
  },
  "parameters": {
    "demand": {
      "symbol": "$$d_k$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{K}|$$",
      "description": "Required amount of cargo for each class $$k$$."
    },
    "capacity": {
      "symbol": "$$A_{t,k}$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{T}| \\times |\\mathcal{K}|$$",
      "description": "Capacity of truck type $$t$$ for cargo class $$k$$."
    },
    "rental_cost_rate": {
      "symbol": "$$c_t$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{T}|$$",
      "description": "Rental cost per kilometer for truck type $$t$$."
    }
  },
  "decision_variables": {
    "truck_count": {
      "symbol": "$$x_t$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{T}|$$",
      "description": "Number of trucks of type $$t$$ to rent as a nonnegative integer."
    }
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "solution": {
    "truck_count": {
      "symbol": "$$x_t$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{T}|$$",
      "description": "Optimal number of trucks of each type to rent."
    },
    "total_cost": {
      "symbol": "$$z$$",
      "shape": "Scalar",
      "description": "Minimum total rental cost, expressed per kilometer."
    }
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "truck_types": ["Type A", "Type B"],
  "cargo_classes": ["refrigerated", "non_refrigerated"],
  "planning_horizon": ["single_period"],
  "demand": {
    "refrigerated": 3000,
    "non_refrigerated": 4000
  },
  "capacity": {
    "Type A": {
      "refrigerated": 20,
      "non_refrigerated": 40
    },
    "Type B": {
      "refrigerated": 30,
      "non_refrigerated": 30
    }
  },
  "rental_cost_rate": {
    "Type A": 30,
    "Type B": 40
  }
}
